<%# The tooltips travel as VALUES on the controller element: Stimulus reads them off
    this.element, and set on the child button they were invisible — the text fell through to
    the English fallback. The wrapper clips daisyUI's tooltip pseudo-element, which causes
    horizontal scroll on a phone. %>
<div class="max-sm:overflow-hidden"
     data-controller="filter-persistence"
     data-filter-persistence-storage-id-value="<%= storage_id %>"
     data-filter-persistence-enabled-value="<%= enabled? %>"
     data-filter-persistence-enabled-tooltip-value="<%= enabled_tooltip %>"
     data-filter-persistence-disabled-tooltip-value="<%= disabled_tooltip %>">
  <%# Explicit aria-label: both icons are `aria-hidden` svgs and the label is only uncovered
      inside the ⋯, so without this the button has no accessible name. It matches the visible
      text so "Label in Name" does not break wherever that label does show.

      `aria-pressed` is the ONLY thing exposing which state it is in: the icon swap is visual
      and `data-tip` is CSS-generated content. Without it the button announces the same on as
      off, and since the click reloads through Turbo announcing nothing, there was no way to
      tell which way it landed. The JS keeps it current (updateUI). %>
  <button type="button"
          class="tooltip tooltip-bottom btn btn-ghost btn-sm gap-2"
          data-action="filter-persistence#toggle"
          data-filter-persistence-target="button"
          data-tip="<%= tooltip %>"
          aria-pressed="<%= enabled? %>"
          aria-label="<%= label %>">
    <span data-filter-persistence-target="iconEnabled" class="<%= 'hidden' unless enabled? %>">
      <%= render Bali::Icon::Component.new('bookmark-check', class: 'w-5 h-5 text-primary') %>
    </span>
    <span data-filter-persistence-target="iconDisabled" class="<%= 'hidden' if enabled? %>">
      <%= render Bali::Icon::Component.new('bookmark', class: 'w-5 h-5 text-base-content/40') %>
    </span>
    <%# No `sm:inline`, on purpose: in the toolbar this is an icon control. Inside the ⋯ the
        control takes a whole row and a bare icon is anonymous there, so the unlayered rule in
        data_table/index.css uncovers it there and only there. `btn-square` is left off the
        button's class for the same reason: it would force width = height and the label would
        overflow. %>
    <span class="toolbar-control-label hidden"><%= label %></span>
  </button>
</div>
